  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Model a torch battery of length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> to be made up of a thin cylindrical bar of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and a concentric thin cylindrical shell of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;filled in between with an electrolyte of resistivity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi></math> (see figure). If the battery is connected to a resistance of value&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, the maximum Joule heating in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> will take place for :</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7ee6d6cf-eeaa-4a49-b14a-698d26e89809-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 268px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
